    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d151">

                <pb facs="0243" n="163" sameAs="frus:frus1936v01/pg163"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A5 Submarines/30½: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-10-06T14:00:00+00:00">October 6, 1936—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 6—9:50 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>462. My despatch No. 2526 September 22, 1936.<anchor n="7" xml:id="d151-f1"/>
                    Foreign Office advises that His Majesty’s Embassy at Rome has been informed by
                    the Italian Government that it proposes to ratify part IV of the London Naval
                    Treaty 1930 early in October. The Foreign Office therefore desires to effect
                    arrangements for early signature of the submarine protocol and has prepared the
                    text of the procès-verbal which is in conformity with that previously
                    transmitted to the Department. Am I authorized to sign and in that case when may
                    I expect to receive my full power?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bingham</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
